## Pedagogical thesis (binding · simple)

```text
A process is something you can describe.
Techniques leave traces: stages, tools, decisions, rejections.
Forms of process come from methods and workplace habits.
Making happens under conditions (brief, time, tools, power).
Meaning of a process is a hypothesis — who it serves, what it hides.
Reception of the outcome remakes the next process.
```

Students leave able to **walk eight steps** on one documented creative process
and to **name Lens A (triad) and Lens B (circulation)**.

Audience: ~19 — **basic enunciations**, guide format, one job per step.

---

## Professor focus (two lenses)

1. **Language / medium / support** — where the *technique* acts (code vs channel vs carrier).  
2. **Communicative circulation** — the process and its outcome move through production →
   recognition → gap → next production (Verón); genre/style/transposition when the
   method or outcome is remade (Steimberg).

Reuse the **pre-analysis** method already in every CT lesson B1
(*How to analyse*). This special unit **deepens** that method into a full guide;
it does not replace it.

Hook **C1–C3** (ideology / labour / GenAI authorship) at least once in the
professor brief or in step 7 examples.

